  "body": "### Summary\nAs a member replying on iPhone, I want a lighter composer: the bottom controls inside the text card and the top buttons as small floating capsules, so that the composer takes less room and looks less heavy.\n\n### Requested (operator, 2026-11-12)\nReference: the message composer of the Claude iOS app (operator's screenshot, kept locally).\n- **Bottom controls inside the card.** Today the control row (\"Vider\", undo, redo on the left; smileys, GIF, image, \"Aa\" on the right) is two separate capsules under the text card. Wanted: these buttons inside the text area's rounded card, on its bottom edge, as the \"+\", model and microphone buttons sit inside the Claude composer.\n- **Top buttons lighter, floating.** Today the top bar has three large round buttons (close ✕, drafts, send ↑) around the title \"Répondre\". Wanted: lighter, floating controls, like the small \"Créer une PR\" capsule floating above the Claude composer.\n- Goal: a much lighter look. Keep the composer simple (the forum's own complexity is not a reason to add UI on iPhone).\n\n### Pointers\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Composer/ComposerHeader.swift` (top bar: close, drafts, title, send; port of `AnswerView.swift` `composerHeader :768-819` @ 87fe0d1c).\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Composer/ComposerControlRow.swift` (control row; port of `composerToolbar :940-1054`).\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Composer/ComposerEditorCard.swift` (the text card), `ComposerHeight.swift` (`ComposerCardLayout.cardHeight`: the card height must include the controls once they move inside).\n- This departs from legacy's layout on purpose: record it as a GAP edit of GAP-653 in the PR's `### Ledger`, and in the legacy pointers' `Differences:`.\n- Related: #592 / #414 (toolbar size, formatting bar), #437, #429.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- iPhone (iOS 27), light and dark, Dynamic Type default and XL: the control buttons sit inside the text card's bottom edge; the card grows with the text up to its cap without hiding them; two lines at XL still fit (today's `ViewThatFits` rule).\n- Close, drafts and send are small floating controls, with the same actions, states (send greyed when empty, spinner while sending) and VoiceOver labels as today.\n- iPad keeps its current composer unless the operator says otherwise.\n- Screenshots before/after on the PR; tests on the layout rules that change.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
